-- the result of the table, computed: the bond graph gives the wrong count for eight of the fourteen
-- compounds. Valine, leucine, isoleucine, glycerol, serine, phenylalanine, 2-butanol and citric acid.
-- It is right for alanine, glycine, threonine, ethanol, 2-propanol and toluene, where the molecule's
-- only symmetries are proper ones -- methyl rotations, ring rotations -- or where the reflection it
-- wrongly allows happens to be supplied by the achiral solvent anyway. So the failure is not sporadic
-- and not universal: it is exactly the failure to distinguish proper from improper operations, and it
-- bites whenever a molecule has a diastereotopic pair.
nmr-graph-wrong : tally-graph-wrong nmr-table ≡ 8
nmr-graph-wrong = λ i → 8
